\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 10. Summary (one-paragraph version)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Implement MCP for kOS as an event-driven, file-backed control system with no persistent processes. A one-shot boot installer installs triggers that react to vessel events and file-based commands. All state is stored in files. All actions are short-lived scripts that read state, act, write results, and exit. There are no daemons, no background loops, no shared memory, and no assumptions of concurrency.}